# Shared local secrets for era-contracts tooling. Copy to `.env` (gitignored)
# and fill in real values. Consumers source this file:
#   - l1-contracts/test/anvil-interop/broadcast-deployer-bundle-to-sepolia.sh
#   - protocol-ops's `dev verify-deployments` (reads via process env)
#   - l1-contracts/test/anvil-interop/src/core/fork-config.ts (reads L2_FORK_URL_*)
#
# Anything checked-in must use placeholders; never put real keys in `.env.example`.

# === L1 RPC + signer ===
# Sepolia (stage / testnet envs) or mainnet (mainnet env). Used by anvil
# `--fork-url`, by `cast send`, and by `dev execute-safe`.
L1_RPC_URL="https://eth-sepolia.g.alchemy.com/v2/<key>"
# Alias the wrapper scripts also accept; same value as L1_RPC_URL when forking.
L1_FORK_URL="${L1_RPC_URL}"
# Deployer EOA private key. Either set DEPLOYER_PK inline or point
# DEPLOYER_PK_FILE at a 0x-hex file (gitignored, e.g. ~/.test_pk).
DEPLOYER_PK_FILE="$HOME/.test_pk"

# Stage Gateway (chain 2708) — settlement layer that uses ZK as base token.
# Use to probe GW-side state during v31 upgrade work.
GW_RPC_URL=

# === Etherscan verification ===
# Used by `protocol_ops dev verify-deployments` (and any `forge verify-contract`
# call) to upload contract source to Etherscan after a real-Sepolia broadcast.
ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=""

# === Per-chain L2 RPCs (anvil-interop fork-mode tests) ===
# fork-config.ts also reads `config/fork-l2-rpcs.json` if it exists. Either
# source is fine; env vars take precedence. Format: L2_FORK_URL_<chainId>.
# Example:
# L2_FORK_URL_270="https://stage.zksync-os.matterhosted.dev/"
# L2_FORK_URL_2702="https://atlas-stage.zksync-os.matterhosted.dev/"
